#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/security.md:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "Trust Model (Required Reading for Open-Source Deployment)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/security.md:13
msgid "FreeAnima is designed for **single-user local / intranet** deployment:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guide/security.md:17
msgid ""
"Habitat RPC REST (`/rpc/v1/*` except health probe/CORS/echo) requires a "
"**Service API Token** (`Authorization: Bearer fa_at_…`); create with `anima "
"token create`. Binding `127.0.0.1` limits network exposure but does not "
"replace token auth — any local process that can reach the port still needs a "
"valid token for business routes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guide/security.md:17
msgid ""
"Default bind is `127.0.0.1`; for LAN access, assess CORS and network "
"isolation yourself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guide/security.md:17
msgid ""
"**Do not** expose the service to the public internet without TLS and token-"
"protected clients (see [`remote-access.md`](remote-access.md))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/security.md:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "Credential Responsibilities"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/security.md:28
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Rule                     | Description                                                                                                                                                          |\n"
"| ------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Sole authoritative store | **Vault** (ECS `vault_item` in User + Agent libraries); legacy pass (`~/.password-store`) is read-only on disk after migration — runtime no longer uses pass CLI     |\n"
"| Never commit secrets     | Do not write API keys, tokens, DB passwords into `config.yaml` and commit to git; runtime LLM/MCP settings live in PG — use `vault()` / `env()` references there too |\n"
"| Runtime directory        | `~/.anima/` (`FREEANIMA_HOME` overridable) holds config, agent machine key (`vault/agent-machine.key`), conversations, memory—recommend `chmod 700`                  |\n"
"| CLI plaintext output     | `anima vault get` prints Agent-library field plaintext to stdout; do not redirect to shared logs                                                                     |\n"
"| User master password     | Set only in Shell `/vault` or bundled Chat unlock box; **never** sent as a chat message or stored in PG messages                                                     |\n"
"| Chat User vault unlock   | **v1 bundled Chat only** (`src/app/shell/web` / desktop / mobile); Discord / WeChat gateways cannot unlock User library                                              |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/security.md:30
msgid ""
"`config.yaml` supports `vault(\"item_id\", \"field\")` (Agent library, "
"Habitat headless) and `env(\"KEY\")` for secrets; values are injected at "
"runtime. Agent tools that need CLI credentials pass per-call `secrets[]` on "
"`terminal_run` / `code_execute` (child env only). Browser form fields use "
"`browser_type` `secret` (typed into the page; never echoed in tool results). "
"User-library resolution still requires an unlocked Chat session on the "
"client."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/guide/security.md:31
#, no-wrap
msgid "Vault trust boundaries"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/security.md:38
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Surface    | User library                                                    | Agent library                                                   |\n"
"| ---------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Habitat PG | Ciphertext + verifier only                                      | Ciphertext + machine key file on disk                           |\n"
"| LLM        | Metadata only; subprocess `secrets[]` / `browser_type` `secret` | Metadata only; subprocess `secrets[]` / `browser_type` `secret` |\n"
"| Shell      | Client master key in memory                                     | Habitat decrypt over loopback SAP                               |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/security.md:39
#, no-wrap
msgid "Data Persistence"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/security.md:46
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Path                               | Content                  | Encryption                      |\n"
"| ---------------------------------- | ------------------------ | ------------------------------- |\n"
"| PostgreSQL conversation archive    | conversations / messages | No application-layer encryption |\n"
"| `~/.anima/vault/agent-machine.key` | Agent vault machine key  | File permissions (`chmod 600`)  |\n"
"| `~/.anima/weixin/`                 | WeChat sync state        | None                            |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/security.md:48
msgid "Disk backup = data access. Protect backup media accordingly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/security.md:49
#, no-wrap
msgid "LLM Tool Risks"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/security.md:62
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Capability                                                 | Risk                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n"
"| ---------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| `terminal_run`                                             | Default `shell: false` (argv spawn). Explicit `shell: true` enables pipes/redirection. Optional `secrets[]` decrypts Vault into **that subprocess env only** (not Habitat `process.env`). Always-on hard deny for catastrophic targets—**not** an OS sandbox; bypass via `code_execute` / interpreters remains |\n"
"| `file_read` / `file_write` / `file_delete` / `file_search` | Path deny: `/etc`, `/proc`, `/sys`, dangerous `/dev`, `~/.ssh` private keys, `FREEANIMA_HOME/vault`. Heuristic deny ≠ writable-root sandbox                                                                                                                                                                    |\n"
"| `code_execute`                                             | No shell (Bun/Node argv). Optional `secrets[]` same as `terminal_run`. Arbitrary JS can still use `node:fs`—not a container sandbox                                                                                                                                                                            |\n"
"| `browser_type`                                             | Optional `secret` decrypts one Vault field and types it into the page; tool result redacts `typed` as `***` (never plaintext)                                                                                                                                                                                  |\n"
"| MCP tools                                                  | Capabilities entirely determined by external Server; stdio default, SSE auth scheme not fully defined                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n"
"| Capability mask (Mask)                                     | Conversation-level tool whitelist; `deny` overrides `allow`; LLM cannot see policy details; see `src/features/task/domain/mask/`                                                                                                                                                                               |\n"
"| ACP (Cursor)                                               | Default **auto-approve** all `session/request_permission` (`allow-once`)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n"
"| `vault_list` / `vault_search` / `vault_get_meta`           | Vault metadata only; no secret values (MCP-exposed)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n"
"| `vault_create` / `vault_update` / `vault_delete`           | Habitat-only (not MCP). create/update seal plaintext into **Agent** library only; tool results are metadata only. User library writes stay in Vault UI                                                                                                                                                         |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/guide/security.md:63
#, no-wrap
msgid "Agent vault usage"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: docs/guide/security.md:69
msgid ""
"**Discover** — `vault_list` / `vault_search` / `vault_get_meta` (metadata "
"only; never plaintext in tool results)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: docs/guide/security.md:69
msgid ""
"**Write (Agent library)** — `vault_create` / `vault_update` / `vault_delete` "
"in Habitat chat only (not MCP). create/update accept plaintext `secrets` to "
"seal on Habitat; results return metadata only. User library: Vault UI."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: docs/guide/security.md:69
msgid ""
"**Use** — pass `secrets: [{ id, env_name, field?, subject_kind? }]` on the "
"same `terminal_run` or `code_execute` call that needs the credential (e.g. "
"`GH_TOKEN` for `gh`); or `secret: { id, field }` on `browser_type` for form "
"fields."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: docs/guide/security.md:69
msgid ""
"**Scope** — plaintext is decrypted for that call only (`secrets[]` → child "
"`env`; `browser_type` `secret` → Camofox type payload). It is **not** "
"written to Habitat `process.env` and **not** returned in tool results. "
"Default `shell=false`: use argv form (`printenv GH_TOKEN`, `gh …`), not "
"`echo $VAR`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/security.md:70
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measures in Place"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/security.md:86
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Measure                    | Description                                                                                                                                                                          |\n"
"| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n"
"| Same-origin RPC            | TanStack Start server functions same-origin by default, no CORS whitelist needed                                                                                                     |\n"
"| Config API secrets         | Habitat config GET returns secrets in cleartext (`api_key`, MCP `env` / `headers`, etc.). Legacy `\"***\"` on write-back is restored via `restoreMaskedSecrets`                        |\n"
"| MCP config                 | `sanitizeConfigForApi` keeps MCP `env` / `headers` plaintext so Habitat MCP page can edit round-trip                                                                                 |\n"
"| File path policy           | Shared `path-policy` for `file_*` tools: `/etc`, vault, ssh private keys, `/proc`/`/sys`, blocked devices                                                                            |\n"
"| Terminal shell default off | `terminal_run` default `shell=false`; pass `shell=true` only when pipes/redirection are needed (friction, not a sandbox)                                                             |\n"
"| Terminal command hard deny | Always-on catastrophic command policy (`terminal-command-policy`); cannot be disabled via env                                                                                        |\n"
"| Slash commands             | Whitelist routing; every command must produce user-visible feedback; long-running commands send an immediate ack then the final result                                               |\n"
"| MCP default stdio          | Reduces port exposure                                                                                                                                                                |\n"
"| Vault isolation            | LLM sees vault item metadata only, not decrypted fields                                                                                                                              |\n"
"| Service API Token          | Habitat RPC REST `/rpc/v1/*` routes require `Authorization: Bearer fa_at_…` (`service_api_tokens` PG table); health probe/CORS/echo exempt. |\n"
"| CI secret scanning         | `.github/workflows/security.yml` (Gitleaks); GitHub Secret scanning + Push protection (free for public repos)                                                                        |\n"
"| `.gitignore`               | `.env.*`, `config.yaml`, private key suffixes                                                                                                                                        |\n"
msgstr ""

